%N A037630 Base-9 digits are, in order, the first n terms of the periodic sequence with initial period 2,3,0.
%H A037630 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (9,0,1,-9).
%F A037630 G.f.: x*(2+3*x) / ( (x-1)*(9*x-1)*(1+x+x^2) ). - _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 21 2011
%F A037630 From _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026: (Start)
%F A037630 a(n) = floor(3*9^(n+1)/104).
%F A037630 a(n) = 9*a(n-1) + a(n-3) - 9*a(n-4). (End)
%t A037630 Table[FromDigits[PadRight[{},n,{2,3,0}],9],{n,20}] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Jan 19 2026 *)
%o A037630 (PARI) a(n) = 3*9^(n+1) \ 104; \\ _Elmo R. Oliveira_, Sep 20 2026
